 an action implicates a flagged subsystem or a player invokes a named rule, retrieve the rule passage from the book before resolving"}, "damage_effect_model": {"policy": "resolve damage/effects from the source-backed derived_formulas; if a required value is missing, block mechanical execution rather than inventing it", "derived_formulas": [{"notes": "Opposed situations use the opponent’s relevant skill/characteristic to set the difficulty level: under 50=Regular, 50+=Hard, 90+=Extreme.", "formula": "target = investigator skill/characteristic, modified by difficulty: Regular=full target, Hard=target/2, Extreme=target/5 (round down)", "field_id": "difficulty_target", "evaluator": "generic"}, {"notes": "From the core rules pages read: if the required success value is 50 or over, only a 100 is a fumble; if below 50, 96-100 is a fumble.", "formula": "if target >= 50 then fumble on 96-100; if target < 50 then fumble on 96-100 only when hard/extreme makes the effective target below 50? (base rule: 96-100 for skills under 50, 100 for skills 50+)", "field_id": "fumble_threshold", "evaluator": "generic"}, {"notes": "Sanity rolls are percentile rolls under current Sanity. Fumbles on SAN can cause maximum loss for the encounter.", "formula": "when a Sanity roll fails, lose the listed Sanity loss for the encounter (often a die expression such as 1D6 or 0/1D6); on a fumble, take the maximum loss", "field_id": "sanity_loss_amount", "evaluator": "generic"}]}, "character_sheet_schema": {"title": "Call Of Cthulhu Keeper Rulebook 40th Anniversary (Sandy Petersen) Character Template", "fields": [{"notes": "Strength; rolled or assigned as percentage value.", "title": "STR", "field_id": "strength", "required": false, "field_type": "stat", "repeatable": false, "visibility": null, "default_value": null, "choices_material_id": null}, {"notes": "Constitution.", "title": "CON", "field_id": "constitution", "required": false, "field_type": "stat", "repeatable": false, "visibility": null, "defau